{"skill":{"slug":"telegram-bot","displayName":"Telegram Bot Builder"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769714362774,"changelog":"Initial release of the Telegram Bot Builder skill.\n\n- Build and manage Telegram bots via the Telegram Bot API.\n- Provides setup instructions and environment variable configuration.\n- Includes commands for sending messages, media, and managing chats/groups.\n- Supports webhooks and polling for bot updates.\n- Features message editing, deletion, forwarding, and keyboard markup examples.\n- Useful code snippets and bash script for launching a simple echo bot.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":8851,"sha256":"6c9a80859b06db0e9b3e4bc226dad357df7b3a1a52e8946eebdf5539f27c5e5c","contentType":null},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2433,"sha256":"e5393d069d0b3f044646595ffb8b83bb4aad6c0ad5ff6303ddde0d6b1cc41065","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789023695033,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"2ed2e993e2beafd3c96b65c45740e2064831d20dcf4d1f34361855809c2b2f3e","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/2ed2e993e2beafd3c96b65c45740e2064831d20dcf4d1f34361855809c2b2f3e","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: telegram-bot\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe OpenClaw AgentSkills skill bundle for 'telegram-bot' is benign. It provides standard `curl` commands and a bash script to interact with the legitimate Telegram Bot API (api.telegram.org). The skill transparently requires `jq`, `curl`, and the `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` environment variable, which are all necessary for its stated purpose. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, obfuscation, or prompt injection attempts against the AI agent. All actions are clearly aligned with building and managing Telegram bots.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160323141},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":26,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":49,"checkedAt":1789023695033},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a straightforward Telegram Bot API helper; its network access and bot-token use are expected, but users should be careful with what they send and with the sample echo bot code.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access to api.telegram.org and use of a Telegram bot token are proportionate to the skill, but the skill can transmit user-selected text, media, documents, chat identifiers, and location data to Telegram.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No installer, dependency download, hidden script, or package execution is present; the metadata only declares required local tools curl and jq plus the TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN environment variable.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The commands are explicit curl examples using placeholders such as CHAT_ID and USER_ID, but they include sensitive operations like sending files/location, deleting messages, banning users, forwarding messages, and a long-running polling example.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"There is no local persistence or privilege escalation, but setWebhook changes persistent Telegram-side bot configuration and the echo-bot example is a foreground infinite polling loop if copied and run.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is building and managing Telegram bots, and the artifact consistently provides Telegram Bot API examples for bot info, messaging, media, webhooks, chat management, and callbacks.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you intend to let the agent operate a Telegram bot with the supplied bot token. Confirm chat IDs, user IDs, files, locations, and moderation actions before running commands, avoid sending secrets or unnecessary personal data through Telegram, and harden the echo-bot sample before using it in production.","findings":"[E1] expected: The repeated external-transmission findings point to api.telegram.org, which is the disclosed and necessary destination for a Telegram Bot API skill rather than hidden exfiltration.\n[SQP-2] expected: Sending messages, files, photos, and location is purpose-aligned, but the artifact would benefit from clearer privacy warnings that this data is sent to Telegram and may reach the selected chat.\n[T09] unexpected: The simple echo bot example interpolates received message text into JSON and iterates updates with shell word splitting; this is an unsafe sample coding pattern, but it is limited to example bot behavior and does not show local command execution, credential theft, or hidden behavior.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789023695033}}}}}